 "note": "Busselton Jetty Interpretive Centre, the four gabled boatsheds on the jetty deck about 50 m out from the beach, from docs/landmarks/jetty_interpretive_centre.md (Landgate aerial, OSM outline, Commons and web photos). Blue weatherboard, white trim, light corrugated roofs, steep gables facing the walkway and the sea; the shore shed has a navy lower wall with the name in plain lettering; a flat white verandah on posts runs along the walkway side of the other three. It stands on the jetty deck: its look sets floor 3.85 (the deck height the base builds). Sized to the OSM outline (26.7 x 11.2 m) so the base's generic sheds (src/core/jetty.ts) stay hidden inside it. Metres: x left to right as seen from the shore end (walkway side to sea side), y back from the shore-facing wall (north-westward along the jetty).",
